# The Docker build context is this directory (App Platform sets it from the
# component's source_dir), and `COPY . .` would otherwise sweep in whatever is
# lying around a developer's checkout.
#
# .env.local is the one that bites, and only started biting now that the
# Dockerfile declares ARG/ENV NEXT_PUBLIC_MARKETING_URL: this checkout's
# .env.local sets it to http://localhost:3001, it is gitignored so it never shows
# up in a diff, and Next loads .env.local AHEAD of the process env. A local or CI
# `docker build` would therefore bake a production image whose every link back to
# the marketing site points at localhost — while the build-args we passed sit
# there, silently overridden. Keep .env.example (documentation only, never read by
# the build).
node_modules
.next
out
.env*
!.env.example
*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.gitignore
*.log
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
